      "id": "tech-https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761",
      "title": "Ask HN: I have been unemployed for 2y. 15 years of experience, US. What to do?",
      "description": "I'm Senior software engineer in the US (DMV area), with 15y of experience. Worked for Fortune 50+ company and bunch of mid-size companies. Been unemployed for 2y and can't find a job, within those 2 years, I pretty much spent my savings that I've saved through years, maybe have 4-5 months left to support my household. Currently, I tutor math and probably about to start working as manager in pizzaria.In Jan 2025, I quit from a mid-size insurance tech company(1000+) after working there for almost 4y, because I was tipped off the they were about to start layoffs and they did. Well, since then I have zero luck finding any job in SWE.At this point, I have massive gap in my resume that I can't explain to recruiters, I can still code (C#/.NET/AWS) and learned the AI, but who cares if date of my last employment is Jan2025. What should I do ?If you have an alternative path (something completely different from SWE or SWE adjacent) that pays \"well\", I would like to hear.\n\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50583761\nPoints: 99\n# Comments: 106",
